{"created": "2026-10-03T01:48:32.173559+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-03T01:48:32.704014+00:00", "id": 23113313, "conceptrecid": "21891383", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23113313", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21891383", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23113313", "metadata": {"title": "An $n^2\\log_2 n-O(n^2)$ lower bound for Hilbert numbers via two-source renewal", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23113313", "publication_date": "2026-10-03", "description": "<p>We construct real planar polynomial vector fields establishing H_hyp(n) &ge; n&sup2; log\u2082 n &minus; Cn&sup2; for every sufficiently large integer n, where C is an absolute constant and H_hyp(n) denotes the supremum of the number of hyperbolic limit cycles among fields of total degree at most n. The construction transplants an existing hyperbolic configuration into a square and prescribes new traces on two adjacent edges, increasing the degree bound by two. A signed tangency condition allows every simple source root to produce reversible centers under the classical quadratic fourfold transformation. Successive common odd-polynomial perturbations yield the degree bound 2m+5 and cycle count 4L+4(m+2)(m+1) from an input field of degree at most m with L selected hyperbolic cycles. A binary degree construction gives the explicit bound L_n &ge; (n+5)&sup2;(log\u2082(n+5) &minus; 25/4) for every n &ge; 3. The selected family contains equal numbers of attracting and repelling cycles. These cycles form nests contained in complete blocks, with a quantified distribution of nest lengths. Further applications concern prescribed polynomial congruences and separated algebraic ovals with prescribed periods and positive nonunit multipliers.</p>\n<p>This version is the frozen submission baseline submission-2026-10-03, exported from commit 4b85f6184ccac8d073de2e1c3c74bd36308f5e58. It contains the 24-page reading PDF, the optional 24-page line-numbered review PDF, the standalone LaTeX source, and a fixed submission package with supplementary finite-algebra scripts, pinned dependencies, matching check records, and SHA-256 manifests. The original 17 manuscript and 8 Han&ndash;Li check groups passed in ordinary and optimized Python modes. These scripts complement the analytical proofs.</p>\n<p>Frozen repository version and package: https://github.com/h-lu/hilbert16-two-source-renewal/releases/tag/submission-2026-10-03</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Lu, Haibo", "affiliation": "Shanghai Institute of Technology"}], "keywords": ["Hilbert's sixteenth problem", "polynomial vector fields", "limit cycles", "Chebyshev pullback", "Melnikov function", "Python", "two-source renewal"], "version": "submission-2026-10-03", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/h-lu/hilbert16-two-source-renewal"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 7, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21891383"}}]}}, "title": "An $n^2\\log_2 n-O(n^2)$ lower bound for Hilbert numbers via two-source renewal", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23113313", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23113313", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23113313?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23113313", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23113313", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23113313", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23113313/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21891383", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21891383", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21891383", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21891383", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23113313/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23113313/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/a